            0.139,
            0.83,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "**4.** Prove that the tangents drawn at the ends of a diameter of a circle are parallel."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.162,
            0.901,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "**5.** Prove that the perpendicular at the point of contact to the tangent to a circle passes through the centre."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.203,
            0.901,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": "**6.** The length of a tangent from a point A at distance 5 cm from the centre of the circle is 4 cm. Find the radius of the circle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.244,
            0.901,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": "**7.** Two concentric circles are of radii 5 cm and 3 cm. Find the length of the chord of the larger circle which touches the smaller circle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.285,
            0.862,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "**8.** A quadrilateral ABCD is drawn to circumscribe a circle (see Fig. 10.12). Prove that"
