            0.546,
            0.901,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "**9.** In Fig. 10.13, XY and X Y  are two parallel tangents to a circle with centre O and another tangent AB with point of contact C intersecting XY at A and $\\mathrm { X ^ { \\prime } Y ^ { \\prime } }$ at B. Prove that $\\angle AOB = 90^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.605,
            0.902,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "**10.** Prove that the angle between the two tangents drawn from an external point to a circle contact at the centre."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.663,
            0.563,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": "**11.** Prove that the parallelogram circumscribing a circle is a rhombus."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.708,
            0.563,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "**12.** A triangle ABC is drawn to circumscribe a circle of radius 4 cm such that the segments BD and DC into which BC is divided by the point of contact D are of lengths 8 cm and 6 cm respectively (see Fig. 10.14). Find the sides AB and AC."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.837,
            0.562,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": "**13.** Prove that opposite sides of a quadrilateral circumscribing a circle subtend supplementary angles at the centre of the circle."
